{
  "layout": "oz_research_vpp_pane",
  "note": "The research module of the OpenZone admin window -- its own pbo and its own layout, because a server without the research mod never loads this file and the core must not know the pane exists. OZL_VppPane.OnCreate builds it under M_SUB_WIDGET and registers it eight times with RegisterPage(research, ...): the rail's pages Overview, Tree, Chains, Point types, Owners, Modules, Statics and Settings all show this one pane, and OnPaneShown switches the page inside it (VPP rework 2026-11-12, design 5.5). The shell moves the root into the content area and sizes it (vpp.content by default); the script reflows the rest (OnWindowResized). Since 2026-11-09 it is the research editor (docs/specs/2026-11-09-research-editor-vpp-design.md): one page per rail entry in RzPages (the script shows one) and the draft's action bar. Names the script resolves by string: every widget named Rz*, ResOwners, ResPicked, ResStatics, RzSummary, GrantType, GrantN, NodeId; ResHint is resolved by the core from the hint name handed to RegisterPage. Captions are stringtable keys of OpenZone_Research (UA original, EN).",
  "root": {"frame": {"name": "PaneResearch", "size": "$vpp.content", "at": [0, 0], "inset": "$vpp.inset",
    "hidden": true, "priority": 2,
    "note": "Hidden: ShowPane shows the open page's pane and hides the rest.",
    "children": [
      {"vbox": {"name": "RzBody", "gap": 8,
        "note": "Vertical budget 680 - 2 * 20 = 640: 574 (pages) + 8 + 28 (action bar) + 8 + 22 (ResHint) = 640. The rail replaced the row of sub-tabs, and its height went to the pages.",
        "children": [
          {"frame": {"name": "RzPages", "h": "fill",
            "note": "The pages lie on top of each other at [0, 0]; the script shows the open sub-tab's page and hides the rest.",
            "children": [

              {"frame": {"name": "RzPage_overview", "w": "fill", "h": "fill",
                "note": "The quick actions that were the whole pane before the editor: factions with their pools, grant, complete a node, reset, reload.",
